Upgrades and Migrations in SYBASE ASE
Upgrades of sybase ase can be done in-place and side-by-side.
In-Place upgrades and patching Steps:
Sybase upgrades
In Sybase we can do upgrades at two levels .
Minor upgrade ex: – upgrading Sybase server to ASE 15.0.3 ESD #1 to ESD #4
Major upgrade eg: – Upgrading Sybase server ASE 12.5 to ASE 15.0.3 / 15.5
Minor Patch upgrades:  we have two methods to do this minor patching .

First Method :
1) Download the EBF binary that we need to apply from SAP Sybase downloads, copy that to the host and Untar it in a Separate location.
2) Take backup of Sybase home ( this would be useful when incase patch fails and we need to rollback.
3) Take backup of all system and user databases
4) Shutdown Backup and ASE server
5) Now run the setup -i console from the untared binary which would prompt for the Sybase home directory and this would overwrite the existing directory and applies the patch. By this step we can say applying patch to the existing verion is completed
6) when you Bring up the Sybase server . Sybase server upgrades all the databases to latest patch level. This we can see by tailing the error .
7) Once the server is up – execute installmaster,installcommit and instmsgs.ebf.

Second Method :
1) Make backup copies of interfaces, runserverfile of both ASE and backup server , config file .
2) take backups of all system and user databases .
3) In this method instead of downloading ebf binary patch . we would get the pre-installed Full version of binary that we are targetting to install
4) copy that full version directory to the location where we have old directory , copy interfaces, runserverfiles and config files to the new directory and start the server . while server comes up it will upgrae the system and userdatabases to new ebf .
5) login to the server and if you see select @@version will show the new ebf .
6) Once the server is up – execute installmaster,installcommit and instmsgs.ebf.

Sybase Major upgrades :
Sybase Major or version upgrades , we can perform this in two ways
1) inplace upgrade
2) dump & load method
In the current environment we always prefer to do the dump & load method only as it will complete with less errors compared to inplace .

Dump and load method is very simple
1) take the backups of all system and user databases
2) shutdown the old server .
3) Build a new instance with new version of binaries, copy the interfaces, configfile
4) sync the logins from old server to new
5) create Sybase devices , create databases, load them with the backups we have ,
6) For configuration changes , use the unix command diff of old conf and new conf and according the prepare the configuration file and reboot ase with it .
